{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966791,"nonce":"/mnCvGhtmZ2f2Gszdv71huHCSU0=","title":"cn::input / cn::textarea CSS `:focus` outline ring transition only plays on the first focus","message":"`.cn-input` and `.cn-textarea` have:\n```css\noutline: 2px solid transparent;\noutline-offset: 1px;\ntransition: outline-color 160ms ease, outline-offset 160ms ease;\n/* :focus sets outline-color to var(--focus-ring), outline-offset to 2px */\n```\n\nFirst focus: outline fades in smoothly (transparent → focus-ring), gap pushes 1 → 2 px.\nBlur: outline fades out.\n**Second focus: outline snaps in with no animation.** Same for subsequent focuses.\n\n\n- The `:focus` rule itself applies on second focus — outline ends at the correct colour and offset.\n- The border-color change (also on `:focus`) DOES animate / take effect correctly.\n- Hover-while-focused now keeps the focus colour (fixed via `router.focused()` lookup in `apply_complex_selector_styles`).\n\n\n1. **Re-ordering apply_css_overrides for FocusedHovered** — base → :hover → :focus so focus wins over hover for the focused_border_color slot. ✓ Fixed border, didn't address ring replay.\n2. **`router.focused()` in `apply_complex_selector_styles::focused_node`** instead of walking element_registry IDs. ✓ Made `:focus` rules match class-only widgets (cn::input has no id). Critical fix — without this nothing matched.\n3. **Adding outline_color / outline_width / outline_offset to `RenderProps::merge_from`** so the Stateful state-callback's `queue_prop_update` doesn't wipe outline back to defaults each fire. Still didn't fix replay.\n\n\n`detect_and_start_transitions` (`renderer/animation/css.rs:641`) compares `before` snapshot to `after` snapshot per-property and only starts a transition when they differ. On second focus:\n- State-callback fires → `final_props.merge_from(callback_props)` → outline now carries through (with our fix).\n- `update_render_props` writes to `render_node.props` — full replace.\n- `apply_complex_selector_styles` runs: snapshots before, applies `:focus`, snapshots after, calls `detect_and_start_transitions`.\n\nThe snapshot `before` at this point already reflects the previous frame's state. If the reverse transition (from blur) was still running OR if the state-callback's prop update brought outline back to focus-ring directly (skipping the transparent base), then `before.outline_color == after.outline_color` → transition skipped → snap.\n\nPlausible additional culprits:\n- `store.transitions[stable_id]` from the reverse transition may not be cleared / finalized between blur and second focus, so the `current_properties` overlay in `check_transition!` short-circuits with the wrong `from`.\n- Base `.cn-input { outline: 2px solid transparent }` IS applied to all matching nodes per-frame by the base-rule re-apply in `apply_complex_selector_styles` (line ~437-451), but ONLY for `prev_affected` nodes. After blur clears `complex_state_affected`, second-focus frame's `prev_affected` is empty — base never re-applies, so before-snapshot is whatever the state-callback / leftover transition left.\n\n\nLive with the snap on second focus. The first focus' animation is the more important one (user just clicked into the input).\n\n\nRe-add the trace at [text_input.rs](crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input.rs) state-callback border-color resolution to confirm `visual` transitions are firing on every focus, then add a trace inside `detect_and_start_transitions` printing `before.outline_color`, `after.outline_color`, and `transition_set.get(\"outline-color\")` to see why the check_transition macro is taking the no-op branch on second focus.\n\n\n- [[gotcha-event-router-layout-id-staleness]] — same router-focus / class-selector area.\n- [[gotcha-first-interaction-skips-class-animation]] — opposite pattern: first interaction broken, subsequent fine. Both point to ordering/race issues between subtree-rebuild and CSS state apply.\n\n**Status**: deferred, 2026-05-23. Revisit when the ring animation feels worth the time vs. the snap-in pop.","files":null}]}